
# Positioning — anchors a floating element (popover / tooltip / dropdown / select / hover-card content) to a reference
# (its trigger). Delegates to @floating-ui/dom, the universal framework-agnostic positioning engine, via `dock`
# (native). The uniform `place` task is the thin Seed layer; the geometry is floating-ui's. This is the dock-delegation
# pattern: own the clean API, delegate the hard math to the proven native library.
#
# `place` computes the (x, y) for `floating` against `reference` at the given placement (e.g. "bottom", "top-start")
# and returns floating-ui's result. The caller applies it to the floating element's style (position: fixed; left: x;
# top: y) and re-runs on scroll / resize for live tracking (floating-ui's autoUpdate). Applying the style needs a dom
# `set-style` primitive (the noted dom follow-up); until then the result is read and applied by the caller.

dock load
  load <@floating-ui/dom>, name floating
  mark native

load @cluesurf/site/code/dom/dom
  find view

task place
  take reference, like view
  take floating, like view
  take placement, like text
  save spot
    call floating/compute-position
      read reference
      read floating
      bind placement, read placement
  send back, read spot
